WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.706
RUFUS: The employee analogy imports all
sorts of assumptions — about the agent

00:00:03.706 --> 00:00:07.412
RUFUS: understanding consequences, about
the agent knowing when something feels
wrong, about the

00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:11.118
RUFUS: agent flagging ambiguous
instructions. None of those apply.

00:00:11.228 --> 00:00:14.815
JAMIE: And in finance, where an agent
making an unexpected decision can have

00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:18.403
JAMIE: systemic consequences — not just
one wrong email, but cascading market
effects

00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:21.990
JAMIE: — the relaxation is extremely
costly.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.863
ALEX: Systemic risk is the technical
term there. It means one failure that

00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:29.557
ALEX: triggers a chain of other failures
across the whole financial system. The

00:00:29.557 --> 00:00:33.250
ALEX: 2008 financial crisis is the most
well-known example of what systemic risk

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.944
ALEX: looks like when it goes wrong.
